			"notes": "# Moblets 0.6.0\n\nMoblets 0.6.0 expands the companion system with Baby Zombies, Baby Endermen, generalized melee equipment, and dedicated spawn eggs for every supported Moblet.\n\n## New companions\n\n- **Baby Zombies** are real vanilla Baby Zombies. Tame them with Raw Chicken, heal them with Rotten Flesh, and equip them with armor plus swords, axes, pickaxes, shovels, or hoes. Once tamed, they can follow or stay, protect their owner, swim, and no longer burn in sunlight.\n- **Baby Endermen** can be tamed with Amethyst Shards and healed with Glow Ink Sacs. They use native unarmed Enderman melee, accept helmets only, and become immune to rain and water damage when tamed. Helmet rendering follows the live Enderman head and includes Patrix / Entity Model Features compatibility.\n\n## Equipment\n\n- Melee Moblet equipment is now capability-driven.\n- Supported companions can use swords, axes, pickaxes, shovels, and hoes.\n- Species such as Baby Endermen remain explicitly unarmed.\n\n## Spawn eggs\n\n- Added 14 dedicated Baby/Moblet spawn eggs covering every supported Moblet.\n- Each egg guarantees its baby variant independently of the configured natural spawn chance.\n- Each Baby egg appears beside its corresponding adult spawn egg.\n- Baby eggs use a smaller inventory presentation while retaining normal held and dropped size."
		},
