			"notes": "# Moblets 0.5.0 for Minecraft 26.1.2\n\nThis build contains the Moblets 0.5.0 feature set backported for Minecraft 26.1.2.\n\nMoblets 0.5.0 introduces a complete in-game configuration system, giving players detailed control over how Moblets spawn, tame, behave, and scale.\n\n## Configuration\n\nMoblets now includes four configuration categories:\n\n### Taming\n- Enable or disable Moblet taming globally.\n- Enable or disable taming per species.\n- Configure individual taming chances.\n\n### Spawning\n- Enable or disable normal Moblet spawning globally.\n- Enable or disable spawning per species.\n- Configure individual spawn-conversion percentages.\n- Configure Pillager Outpost Moblets and their target count.\n\n### Encounters\nConfigure special Moblet encounters including:\n- Pillager Outposts\n- Wandering Trader caravans\n- Snow Golem companions\n- Iron Golem companions\n- Baby Camel Husk riders\n\n### Advanced\n- Separate Wild and Tamed Moblet profiles.\n- Configure Health, Damage, Movement Speed, and ranged spread where applicable.\n- Attribute percentages are displayed relative to the corresponding vanilla adult mob.\n- Configure Creeper explosion damage and blast radius.\n- Per-Moblet and global Advanced resets.\n\n## Loader Support\n\nThe configuration GUI is available through each loader's normal interface:\n\n- Fabric: Mod Menu -> Moblets -> Configure\n- Forge: Mods -> Moblets -> Config\n- NeoForge: Mods -> Moblets -> Config\n\nAll loaders use the same Moblets configuration system and `config/moblets.json`.\n\n## Balance\n\nTamed Skeleton-family Moblets now use a consistent health baseline of 175% of their vanilla adult counterpart:\n\n- Skeleton\n- Stray\n- Bogged\n- Parched\n- Wither Skeleton\n\n## Friendly Mob Behavior\n\n- Iron Golems no longer target tamed Moblets.\n- Snow Golems no longer target tamed Moblets.\n- Wolves no longer target tamed Skeleton-family Moblets.\n- Tamed Skeleton-family Moblets no longer flee from Wolves.\n- Follow Owner now works normally around Wolves.\n- Wild Skeleton-family Moblets retain their normal Wolf interactions."
		}
